        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "[codex] Stabilize Antigravity PTY output tests",
        "body": "## Summary\n- Wait for the Antigravity PTY descriptor probe to finish writing both output lines before asserting.\n- Apply the same stabilization to the macOS and Linux copies of the test so both lanes avoid the same partial-file read race.\n\n## Behavior proof\nA macOS CI shard previously observed the probe output after `pwd > result.txt` but before the descriptor status append completed:\n\n```text\nExpectation failed: (lines → [\"/Users/runner\"]) == ([NSHomeDirectory(), \"closed\"] → [\"/Users/runner\", \"closed\"])\n± removed [\"closed\"]\n```\n\nThe probe script writes the working directory first, then appends `closed` or `inherited`. Waiting only for `result.txt` to exist can read the first line early, so the tests now poll until both lines are present before the final exact assertion.\n\nAfter-fix focused test output, run locally on branch `c5b3a0587f92` after rebasing onto `daba50847e18`:\n\n```text\n$ swift test --no-parallel --filter '(^CodexBarTests\\.AntigravityCLISessionTests/)'\n...\n✔ Test \"pty launcher uses home and closes unrelated descriptors\" passed after 0.013 seconds.\n...\n✔ Suite AntigravityCLISessionTests passed after 0.039 seconds.\n✔ Test run with 48 tests in 1 suite passed after 0.040 seconds.\n```\n\n## Validation\n- `swift test --no-parallel --filter '(^CodexBarTests\\.AntigravityCLISessionTests/)'`\n- `.build/lint-tools/bin/swiftformat Tests/CodexBarTests/AntigravityCLISessionTests.swift TestsLinux/AntigravityProcessLauncherLinuxTests.swift --lint`\n- `.build/lint-tools/bin/swiftlint --strict Tests/CodexBarTests/AntigravityCLISessionTests.swift TestsLinux/AntigravityProcessLauncherLinuxTests.swift`\n- `.build/lint-tools/bin/swiftlint --strict`\n- `git diff --check`",
